## Request Interceptors

### Token Propagation Interceptor

```java
@Slf4j
@Component
public class TokenPropagationInterceptor implements ClientHttpRequestInterceptor {
    
    @Override
    public ClientHttpResponse intercept(
            HttpRequest request,
            byte[] body,
            ClientHttpRequestExecution execution) throws IOException {
        
        var authentication = SecurityContextHolder.getContext().getAuthentication();
        
        if (authentication instanceof JwtAuthenticationToken jwtAuth) {
            var token = jwtAuth.getToken().getTokenValue();
            request.getHeaders().setBearerAuth(token);
            log.debug("Propagating JWT token to {}", request.getURI().getHost());
        }
        
        return execution.execute(request, body);
    }
}
```

### Correlation ID Interceptor

```java
@Component
public class CorrelationIdInterceptor implements ClientHttpRequestInterceptor {
    
    private static final String CORRELATION_ID_HEADER = "X-Correlation-Id";
    
    @Override
    public ClientHttpResponse intercept(
            HttpRequest request,
            byte[] body,
            ClientHttpRequestExecution execution) throws IOException {
        
        var correlationId = MDC.get("correlationId");
        
        if (correlationId != null) {
            request.getHeaders().set(CORRELATION_ID_HEADER, correlationId);
        }
        
        return execution.execute(request, body);
    }
}
```

### HTTP Logging Interceptor

```java
@Slf4j
@Component
public class HttpLoggingInterceptor implements ClientHttpRequestInterceptor {
    
    @Override
    public ClientHttpResponse intercept(
            HttpRequest request,
            byte[] body,
            ClientHttpRequestExecution execution) throws IOException {
        
        var startTime = System.currentTimeMillis();
        
        log.debug("HTTP Request: {} {}", request.getMethod(), request.getURI());
        
        ClientHttpResponse response = null;
        try {
            response = execution.execute(request, body);
            return response;
        } finally {
            var duration = System.currentTimeMillis() - startTime;
            var statusCode = response != null ? response.getStatusCode().value() : 0;
            
            log.info("HTTP Response: {} {} - Status: {} - Duration: {}ms",
                request.getMethod(),
                request.getURI(),
                statusCode,
                duration);
        }
    }
}
```

## Using Clients in Handlers

```java
@Slf4j
@Service
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class EModalSearchStrategy implements ContainerSearchStrategy {
    
    private final EModalClient eModalClient;
    private final EModalFeeDetailsService feeDetailsService;
    
    @Override
    @CircuitBreaker(name = "emodal", fallbackMethod = "searchFallback")
    @Retry(name = "emodal")
    public Result<List<ContainerSearchResult>> search(String containerNumber, TradeType tradeType) {
        log.debug("Searching eModal for container: {}", containerNumber);
        
        var inventory = eModalClient.getContainerFeeInventory(
            containerNumber, 
            tradeType.getCode()
        );
        
        if (inventory.isEmpty()) {
            return Result.failure(DomainErrors.CONTAINER_NOT_FOUND);
        }
        
        // Enrich with fee details
        var results = inventory.stream()
            .map(item -> {
                var feeDetails = feeDetailsService.getFeeDetails(item.drayUnitId());
                return ContainerSearchResult.from(item, feeDetails);
            })
            .toList();
        
        return Result.success(results);
    }
    
    private Result<List<ContainerSearchResult>> searchFallback(
            String containerNumber, TradeType tradeType, Throwable t) {
        log.error("eModal search failed, circuit breaker fallback: {}", t.getMessage());
        return Result.failure(DomainErrors.EMODAL_UNAVAILABLE);
    }
}
```

## Parallel Calls with Virtual Threads

```java
public Result<BulkContainerSearchResult> handle(BulkSearchContainersQuery query) {
    // Execute searches in parallel - virtual threads handle blocking efficiently
    var futures = query.containerIds().stream()
        .map(containerId -> CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(
            () -> searchSingle(containerId, query.backend(), query.tradeType())
        ))
        .toList();
    
    // Wait for all to complete
    CompletableFuture.allOf(futures.toArray(new CompletableFuture[0])).join();
    
    // Collect results
    var searchResults = futures.stream()
        .map(CompletableFuture::join)
        .toList();
    
    return Result.success(aggregateResults(searchResults));
}
```

## Connection Pooling (Apache HttpClient)

For high-throughput scenarios:

```java
@Configuration
public class HttpClientConfig {
    
    @Bean
    public ClientHttpRequestFactory clientHttpRequestFactory() {
        var connectionManager = PoolingHttpClientConnectionManagerBuilder.create()
            .setMaxConnTotal(100)      // Max total connections
            .setMaxConnPerRoute(20)    // Max per route
            .setDefaultConnectionConfig(
                ConnectionConfig.custom()
                    .setConnectTimeout(5, TimeUnit.SECONDS)
                    .setSocketTimeout(30, TimeUnit.SECONDS)
                    .build()
            )
            .build();
        
        var httpClient = HttpClients.custom()
            .setConnectionManager(connectionManager)
            .evictIdleConnections(30L, TimeUnit.SECONDS)
            .build();
        
        return new HttpComponentsClientHttpRequestFactory(httpClient);
    }
}
```

## Conventions

- ALWAYS use `RestClient`, NOT `RestTemplate` (deprecated)
- Use **declarative HTTP interfaces** for all backend clients
- Configure timeouts explicitly (connect: 5s, read: 30s recommended)
- Use interceptors for cross-cutting concerns (auth, logging, correlation IDs)
- Enable virtual threads for optimal blocking I/O performance
- Apply Resilience4j decorators (`@CircuitBreaker`, `@Retry`) at strategy level
- Log outgoing requests with correlation IDs
- Backend DTOs end with `Dto` suffix and go in `client/{backend}/dto/`
- Client interfaces end with `Client` suffix

**See also:** `bff-architecture.mdc`, `resilience.mdc`, `testing.mdc`
